From 317d6fae595d1ba6fb9be1fcd3fa55597c9b3c6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Alba Vives <sebasjosue84@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Apr 2026 12:04:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add Secure Storage MMIO device for Root of Trust

Custom QEMU device at 0x10200000 that provides 8 slots of 64 bytes
each for the RoT firmware to store crypto keys and other secrets.

Register-based interface: CMD, STATUS, SLOT_ID, OFFSET, SIZE, DATA.
Supports WRITE, READ, ERASE, and STATUS commands. Data is transferred
4 bytes at a time through the DATA register.

Integrated into the RISC-V virt machine memmap so the firmware can
access it like any other MMIO peripheral.
---
 hw/misc/meson.build      |   3 +
 hw/misc/secure_storage.c | 291 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/riscv/virt.c          |   4 +
 include/hw/riscv/virt.h  |   1 +
 4 files changed, 299 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/misc/secure_storage.c

